    "notes": "I implemented the spec in `src/lib.rs`. Every test passes: 45 of 45 in the public suite and 110 of 110 in the private suite. The build gives no warnings, and none of the tests contradicted the spec.\n\n- **`parse_duration`**: trims the text with `str::trim`, then reads each component as ASCII digits followed by a unit. A count cannot have a leading zero unless it is just `0`. When reading the unit it checks for `ms` before `m`. Units must come in the order d, h, m, s, ms, each at most once. All the arithmetic is checked, so a total above 2^53 − 1, or a count too big for a `u64`, returns `InvalidDuration` instead of panicking or wrapping around. Empty text, a number with no unit, or anything left over is rejected.\n- **`format_duration`**: rejects anything above 9007199254740991 with `MillisecondsOutOfRange`. It returns `\"0ms\"` for zero; otherwise it builds the string from the largest unit down and leaves out zero components.\n- **Error messages**: parse errors contain \"duration\" and format errors contain \"milliseconds\", as the spec requires.\n\nTests left failing: none",
